!
! Period-averaged (SVEA) 1D example.  Seeded, planar undulator, no lattice.
!
! The options below are the ordinary ones - see any other example in
! inputs/simple/ for the full annotated list, or the user manual in $PUFFIN/doc/
! - so this header only covers what makes this deck an averaged one.
!
!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------!
!                      PERIOD-AVERAGED MODE
!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------!
!
! qAveraged          .true. integrates the field as a slowly varying envelope
!                    about the resonant carrier exp(-i z2 / 2 rho) instead of
!                    resolving the carrier on the mesh.  The undulator period
!                    is averaged over, so neither the mesh nor the step has to
!                    resolve it, which is where the speed comes from.
!
! lambdarPerCell     z2 mesh spacing, in resonant wavelengths.  This REPLACES
!                    nodesPerLambdar, which sizes the z2 mesh only when
!                    qAveraged is .false. and is ignored here.  1.0 is the
!                    recommendation; 2 is fine, 4 is tolerable before
!                    saturation, 8 is not.  See benchmark/averaged/README.md.
!
! What the two together buy on this deck: dz2 = 4 pi rho lambdarPerCell, so at
! rho = 0.005 and lambdarPerCell = 1 the 60-unit z2 model takes 956 nodes,
! where nodesPerLambdar = 12 unaveraged takes 10506 - 11x fewer - and the step
! below is 2 per undulator period rather than 30.
!
!
!                      WHAT AVERAGED MODE WILL NOT DO
!
! Checked at setup (chkAveraged, puffin/lib/setup/checks.f90) and refused
! rather than silently approximated:
!
!   - qResume, field_file (an HDF5 field) and HDF5/MASP macroparticle input.
!     A resolved field read into an envelope array, or a pperp that still
!     carries the quiver, would be wrong rather than obviously wrong.
!   - A seed detuned past the envelope mesh's band, roughly
!     1 +/- 1/(2 lambdarPerCell).  freqf = 1.0 below is on resonance.
!
! A beam whose energy spread or oscillation reaches past that band warns rather
! than stops: its tails are out of band, which makes the run partly wrong, not
! invalid.
!
!
!                      COST AND ACCURACY
!
! These are the parameters of the averaged-vs-unaveraged comparison deck in
! benchmark/averaged/, so the accuracy here is measured rather than asserted:
! a CLARA-like 1D case, seeded and noise-free, 60 periods, about 3.8 gain
! lengths and still exponential.
!
! Cost, measured on this deck at 2 ranks: 6.2 s as it stands, against 27.4 s
! with qAveraged = .false. and the unaveraged mesh and step (nodesPerLambdar
! = 12, stepsPerPeriod = 30).  The field mesh shrinks 11x but the 1D cost is
! largely the macroparticles, so the run gets 4.5x faster rather than 11x.
! Bigger wins are in benchmark/averaged/README.md - 9.3x on the seeded helical
! case, and 12x on a SASE run to saturation against the unaveraged solver's own
! default mesh, 44x against a converged one.
!
! Accuracy on a PLANAR undulator, which is what this deck is, carries a ~1%
! power remainder that helical does not: a planar undulator radiates harmonics
! and a single averaged envelope cannot hold them.  See #130 and the harmonic
! decomposition in benchmark/averaged/README.md.  Helical is tighter - 0.2% at
! this cell size, limited by the cell and not the step.  The SASE study's gain
! length comes within 0.2% of a converged unaveraged reference.
!
! Known remainders and what is not modelled yet are in
! AVERAGED_MODE_ROADMAP.md.
!
!
! Begin input:-

&MDATA
 qOneD                  = .true.
 qFieldEvolve           = .true.
 qElectronsEvolve       = .true.
 qElectronFieldCoupling = .true.
 qFocussing             = .false.
 qDiffraction           = .false.
 qFilter                = .true.
 q_noise                = .false.
 qUndEnds               = .false.
 qAveraged              = .true.
 lambdarPerCell         = 1.0
 beam_file              = 'beam_file.in'
 sElectronThreshold     = 0.05
 iNumNodesX             = 1
 iNumNodesY             = 1
 nodesPerLambdar        = 12        ! ignored: qAveraged uses lambdarPerCell
 sFModelLengthX         = 4.0
 sFModelLengthY         = 4.0
 sFModelLengthZ2        = 60.0
 iRedNodesX             = 1
 iRedNodesY             = 1
 sFiltFrac              = 0.3
 sDiffFrac              = 1.0
 sBeta                  = 1.0
 seed_file              = 'seed_file.in'
 srho                   = 0.005
 sux                    = 1.0
 suy                    = 1.0
 saw                    = 1.0121809
 sgamma_r               = 456.40
 lambda_w               = 0.0275
 zundType               = 'planepole'
 taper                  = 0.0
 lattFile               = ''
 stepsPerPeriod         = 2         ! 1 is converged too; 30 is usual unaveraged
 nPeriods               = 60
 sZ0                    = 0.0
 iWriteNthSteps         = 20
 iWriteIntNthSteps      = 2         ! one integrated write per undulator period
 /
